                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "54945adf-2db7-35ef-a3dd-0ffd72e12939",
                        "entry_id": "09e0e70c-c698-3ac0-94bd-ae37bd221a9c",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Présenter comme héroïque."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "1a387eb0-a72e-4248-8a3b-d8e75145b2d9",
                        "source_entry_id": "09e0e70c-c698-3ac0-94bd-ae37bd221a9c",
                        "source_sense_id": "54945adf-2db7-35ef-a3dd-0ffd72e12939",
                        "target_lang_word": "heroicise",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "heroicise",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0673cbcc-6798-393b-8b4b-912cdc07a160",
                                        "entry_id": "a99f527d-9fe5-3695-b4e1-aac8c86212b4",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Alternative form of heroicize."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "alt-of",
                                            "alternative"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "675f2ea4-d76c-4c1e-8975-524b806fb632",
                                                "sense_id": "0673cbcc-6798-393b-8b4b-912cdc07a160",
                                                "text": "In La Route des Flandres, Blum's scepticism counters George's persistent, if ultimately defeated tendency to heroicise and idealise the family past."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6124fee8-3c46-4b00-a76e-fa2bc900d608",
                                                "sense_id": "0673cbcc-6798-393b-8b4b-912cdc07a160",
                                                "text": "The archly staged 'landing' scenes from this work in particular both sanitise and heroicise the encounter between Britons and 'Natives' in ways that later Britons could, in turn, see as both confirmation of a worthy purpose and a form of transaction, if not transfiguration, that might validate their presence in the distant colonial landscape."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c88ad459-cf9b-4882-9e67-ea9b30418db4",
                                                "sense_id": "0673cbcc-6798-393b-8b4b-912cdc07a160",
                                                "text": "Both forms have a specific resonance in Russia, albeit for quite different reasons: the war film was used in Soviet times first as a means to heroicise the state, and later to heroicise the soldier (he, in most cases, would give his life for the fatherland)."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "d82e0ce8-151b-41f0-9a1b-0d58baeb0934",
                        "source_entry_id": "09e0e70c-c698-3ac0-94bd-ae37bd221a9c",
                        "source_sense_id": "54945adf-2db7-35ef-a3dd-0ffd72e12939",
                        "target_lang_word": "heroicize",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "heroicize",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9177a8da-6392-3b38-90b9-89d1f0f57689",
                                        "entry_id": "ac72f327-ea9c-3651-a4ba-d20c1fee7056",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To make or depict as heroic."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bcaa26ff-55ee-47dc-99a9-6e5b670d406d",
                                                "sense_id": "9177a8da-6392-3b38-90b9-89d1f0f57689",
                                                "text": "A strong tendency to heroicize death prevailed in the nihilism of the Third Reich."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5df3ca25-ab61-4985-84c1-ab1d44e19b93",
                                                "sense_id": "9177a8da-6392-3b38-90b9-89d1f0f57689",
                                                "text": "Professors of post-coloniality have a curious need to heroicize (and self-heroicize) and these Australians are no exception."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1c499b3f-362c-48ea-9ea0-a3329eff12d3",
                                                "sense_id": "9177a8da-6392-3b38-90b9-89d1f0f57689",
                                                "text": "Societies heroicize soldiers during war to encourage young men to enlist and their families to support the war effort."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "07ac6615-43be-445f-b96b-2156c8c330b8",
                        "source_entry_id": "09e0e70c-c698-3ac0-94bd-ae37bd221a9c",
                        "source_sense_id": "54945adf-2db7-35ef-a3dd-0ffd72e12939",
